I’ll inspect the repository’s source, configuration, and existing documentation, then write a README grounded only in what the project actually supports.
The project is a Linux-oriented interactive launcher, not a single standalone scanner: its menu installs and invokes a broad set of third-party tools, many through shell commands and often with `sudo`. I’m documenting the supported launch paths and calling out those operational and authorization risks rather than implying every listed tool works out of the box.
Created `README.md` with repository-grounded setup instructions, usage notes, tool categories, Docker configuration details, and safety and licensing guidance. No other files were changed.

